# ===========================================
# RSYNC EXCLUDES FOR: make push (Local → HA)
# MORE RESTRICTIVE - Protect HA's runtime state!
# ===========================================

# Database and log files
home-assistant_v2.db*
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log*

# custom_components: allow cradlewise through, protect everything else.
# The parent directory must be explicitly included so rsync descends into it.
# `+` rules win by first-match, so cradlewise syncs while the trailing `**`
# exclude shields all other components (sibling dirs AND loose files) from
# --delete — preserving HACS/other integrations on the remote.
+ custom_components/
+ custom_components/cradlewise/
+ custom_components/cradlewise/**
- custom_components/**
custom_icons/
themes/

# Runtime/cache directories
.cloud/
deps/
tts/
.uuid
__pycache__/

# Large directories not needed for config management
backups/
image/
tmp_backups/
www/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp

# ===========================================
# CRITICAL: NEVER PUSH .storage/ TO HA
# These contain runtime state that HA manages:
# - Integration configs (Shelly, Tuya, etc.)
# - Entity/device registries (renames, disables)
# - Dashboards created via UI
# - Authentication and sessions
# All changes should be made via HA UI or API
# ===========================================
.storage/
